  "description": "Plugin control bridge (steer/continuation/interrupt), post-turn triggers, cooperative flags, live adviser events, a preserved card at the turn end, labeled adviser-triggered turns, and adviser rows on every host surface: Desktop card, TUI card, classic CLI block, web session inspector, and a native web chat transcript (the PTY stays available as a fallback); each adviser note carries its own severity on every surface; and the CLI's verbose tool progress prints each call's result body under its row, with the one-line modes as the fold; and a tool step's reasoning prints above the rows it asked for, never under the final answer; and a plugin callback may declare its own hook budget so a pre-tool gate can wait for one model answer without slowing every other hook. It also lets the minir memory plugin switch off the host's built-in MEMORY.md and USER.md stores through memory.minir.block_builtin_memory (on by default inside its own block), so the two native files are neither loaded nor rendered.",
